      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.049,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.087,
            0.637,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "Is the black-and-white region in Fig. 6.14 tileable?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "Any region tiled with black-and-white-tiles must have an equal number of black tiles and white tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.155,
            0.847,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": "Since the black-and-white region in Fig. 6.14 has 8 white squares and 6 black squares, it can never be tiled with these tiles!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.209,
            0.802,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": "Use this idea to find another unit square that, when removed from a 5 × 3 grid, makes it non-tileable?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.202,
            0.904,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_24_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.254,
            0.848,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "Isn’t it surprising how, by introducing colours and making the problem more complicated, it becomes easier to tackle? What a creative way of looking at the problem!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.322,
            0.316,
            0.347
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.349,
            0.485,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": "Are the following tilings possible?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.382,
            0.183,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.425,
            0.385,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "Region to be tiled"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.522,
            0.183,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "2."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.376,
            0.841,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_24_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.74,
            0.391,
            0.761
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Tiling the Entire Plane"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.77,
            0.846,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "So far we have seen how to tile a given region. What about tiling the entire plane?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.823,
            0.773,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": "Can you think of a shape whose copies can tile the entire plane? Clearly, squares can."
        },
        {
